libfive-wasm carried patch 0005: single-threaded mesher under Emscripten

libfive's mesher spawns std::async tasks even when settings.workers == 1. The
wasm baseline has no pthreads (AD-008), and Emscripten's thread stubs fail at
runtime, so every reachable worker-pool, dual-walk, object-pool and BRep-merge
call site runs inline under __EMSCRIPTEN__. Native builds keep upstream's
asynchronous paths for the future --host=native cross-check.

Serves AD-008 (portable, thread-free baseline) and AD-014 (single-threaded
kernel). Do not edit the vendored tree; edit this patch and bump patch_digest
in vendor/libfive.lock.

